weighted total is far below 183). That means you will generally not be a U.S. tax resident for 2024 and 
can claim Singapore tax residence instead. You may still need to file Form 1040-NR for any U.S.-source 
income; keep travel and pay/withholding records and consult a cross-border tax advisor for filing 
details.

